---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/site.css";
import "../styles/controls.css";
import ApprovalRoute from "../components/app/ApprovalRoute.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Controls · Meridian"
  description="The rules Meridian's workflow enforces on every partner funding request: who can approve, what must be in place before signing and paying, what is kept, and who can see what."
  share="og-controls.png"
  shareAlt="Meridian: Rules the workflow enforces and records. An example request, MDF-000033: its Approve button is blocked by rule C-01, because you submitted it."
>

<main id="main">

<!-- 1 · Hero: words left, a rule you can try to break right -->
<section class="khero" id="top"><div class="in khero-grid">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <span class="pill">Controls</span>
    <h1>Rules the workflow <em>enforces and records.</em></h1>
    <p class="lead">They aren't policies to remember. Some rules the workflow checks at the moment they matter, so they can't be skipped. The rest are kept on the record, and every decision goes on the record too.</p>
    <div class="btns"><a class="btn" href="#rules">See every rule</a><a class="btn ghost" href="/audit-evidence-pack">See them on a record</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="ktry rose halo" id="tryBox"><span class="sheet" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="card kmock">
      <p class="kmock-t"><b class="mono">MDF-000033</b> is waiting for approval.</p>
      <dl class="kv"><div><dt>Submitted by</dt><dd>You</dd></div><div><dt>Amount</dt><dd class="mono">USD 24,000</dd></div></dl>
      <button type="button" class="kbtn" id="tryApprove">Approve</button>
      <span class="ktip">You submitted this request</span>
    </div>
    <div class="chip kchip"><i class="kx" aria-hidden="true">✕</i>Blocked by rule <b class="mono">C-01</b></div>
    <p class="khint" id="tryHint" aria-live="polite">Nobody approves a request they submitted or edited.</p>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- 2 · Every rule: the heading stays on the left; on the right, one column that opens a group at a time -->
<section class="sec" id="rules" aria-labelledby="h-rules"><div class="in kcols">
  <div class="khead"><h2 id="h-rules" class="rv">Every rule,<br><em>in plain words.</em></h2><p class="lead rv">19 controls, grouped by the question they answer. Eight are checks the workflow enforces, marked Enforced. The rest describe what is checked and kept on the record.</p><p class="knote rv">These are controls built into the workflow. Security attestations are a separate subject.</p></div>
  <div class="kacc">
      <details class="kt rose pv" name="rules" open>
        <summary><h3>Who can approve</h3><span class="kn">5 rules</span><i class="kplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
        <ul>
        <li class="kc" id="c-01"><b class="mono">C-01</b><span>The person who submitted or edited a request cannot approve it.</span><i class="kenf">Enforced</i></li>
        <li class="kc" id="c-02"><b class="mono">C-02</b><span>One person takes at most one approval step on a request per round.</span><i class="kenf">Enforced</i></li>
        <ApprovalRoute />
        <li class="kc" id="c-03"><b class="mono">C-03</b><span>A step accepts only the role it names, with a minimum number of different approvers.</span><i class="kenf">Enforced</i></li>
        <li class="kc" id="c-04"><b class="mono">C-04</b><span>Approval steps are selected by amount and funding recommendation, from the published route.</span></li>
        <li class="kc" id="c-05"><b class="mono">C-05</b><span>Approval records the amount, the period and any conditions.</span></li></ul>
      </details>
      <details class="kt mint pv" name="rules">
        <summary><h3>Before anything is signed</h3><span class="kn">3 rules</span><i class="kplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
        <ul>
        <li class="kc" id="c-06"><b class="mono">C-06</b><span>Nothing is signed before the campaign references are recorded.</span><i class="kenf">Enforced</i></li>
        <li class="kc" id="c-07"><b class="mono">C-07</b><span>The countersignature follows the partner's signature.</span><i class="kenf">Enforced</i></li>
        <li class="kc" id="c-08"><b class="mono">C-08</b><span>An activity is Ready only with both signatures, a current purchase order and campaign references.</span><i class="kenf">Enforced</i></li></ul>
      </details>
      <details class="kt peach pv" name="rules">
        <summary><h3>Before anything is paid</h3><span class="kn">4 rules</span><i class="kplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
        <ul>
        <li class="kc" id="c-09"><b class="mono">C-09</b><span>Proof is reviewed file by file and cost line by cost line, against the activity type's checklist.</span></li>
        <li class="kc" id="c-10"><b class="mono">C-10</b><span>Costs are converted at your published monthly exchange rates.</span></li>
        <li class="kc" id="c-11"><b class="mono">C-11</b><span>The invoice must equal the confirmed claim amount exactly.</span><i class="kenf">Enforced</i></li>
        <li class="kc" id="c-12"><b class="mono">C-12</b><span>Only approved invoices reach accounts payable, stamped with who approved them.</span></li></ul>
      </details>
      <details class="kt butter pv" name="rules">
        <summary><h3>What is kept</h3><span class="kn">3 rules</span><i class="kplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
        <ul>
        <li class="kc" id="c-13"><b class="mono">C-13</b><span>Every decision is stored with the person, their role and the time.</span></li>
        <li class="kc" id="c-14"><b class="mono">C-14</b><span>Uploaded files are fingerprinted and cannot be altered after upload. A correction is a new file; the original stays on the record.</span></li>
        <li class="kc" id="c-15"><b class="mono">C-15</b><span>Each request keeps the form and approval-route version it was submitted under.</span></li></ul>
      </details>
      <details class="kt rose pv" name="rules">
        <summary><h3>Who can see what</h3><span class="kn">4 rules</span><i class="kplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
        <ul>
        <li class="kc" id="c-16"><b class="mono">C-16</b><span>Partners never see internal notes, reasons, budgets or other partners.</span><i class="kenf">Enforced</i></li>
        <li class="kc" id="c-17"><b class="mono">C-17</b><span>The explanation shown to the partner is stored apart from internal reasons.</span></li>
        <li class="kc" id="c-18"><b class="mono">C-18</b><span>Each customer's data is isolated. Access is granted per person, per Workspace, per role.</span></li>
        <li class="kc" id="c-19"><b class="mono">C-19</b><span>Meridian staff set up your organization and have no access to your business records.</span></li></ul>
      </details>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- 3 · Why: three sourced reasons, each tied to the rules that answer it -->
<section class="sec" id="why" aria-labelledby="h-why"><div class="in">
  <div class="sec-c"><h2 id="h-why" class="rv">Why these <em>rules exist.</em></h2><p class="lead rv">Regulators and accounting standards already expect them.</p></div>
  <ul class="wy">
    <li class="wyc pv"><span class="pill">Separate duties</span><p>The DOJ and SEC's guide to the Foreign Corrupt Practices Act lists segregation of duties among the internal controls it expects.</p>
      <div class="wya"><a class="tag ctl" href="#c-01">C-01</a><a class="tag ctl" href="#c-02">C-02</a><a class="tag ctl" href="#c-03">C-03</a></div>
      <a class="lk" href="https://www.justice.gov/criminal-fraud/file/1292051/download" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FCPA Resource Guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>
    <li class="wyc pv"><span class="pill">Proof before payment</span><p>In 2022 the SEC found that a large software vendor's subsidiaries approved marketing reimbursements under USD 5,000 without evidence the activity took place.</p>
      <div class="wya"><a class="tag ctl" href="#c-08">C-08</a><a class="tag ctl" href="#c-09">C-09</a><a class="tag ctl" href="#c-11">C-11</a></div>
      <a class="lk" href="https://www.sec.gov/files/litigation/admin/2022/34-95913.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SEC order 34-95913 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>
    <li class="wyc pv"><span class="pill">Expense or revenue</span><p>Under ASC 606 and IFRS 15, a payment to a partner counts as a marketing expense only for a distinct service, and only up to that service's fair value. The rest reduces revenue.</p>
      <div class="wya"><a class="tag ctl" href="#c-09">C-09</a><a class="tag ctl" href="#c-10">C-10</a><a class="tag ctl" href="#c-14">C-14</a></div>
      <a class="lk" href="https://viewpoint.pwc.com/dt/us/en/pwc/accounting_guides/revenue_from_contrac/revenue_from_contrac_US/chapter_4_determinin_US/46consideration_paya_US.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PwC on ASC 606 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>
  </ul>
</div></section>

<!-- 4 · Proof: one sheet of glass, with the checks a record carries -->
<section class="sec kproof-s" aria-labelledby="h-proof"><div class="in">
  <div class="kproof pv">
    <span class="blob kb1"></span><span class="blob kb2"></span>
    <div class="kglass">
      <div class="kp-w"><h2 id="h-proof">Every decision <em>leaves a mark.</em></h2><p class="lead">Each one is on the record: who, in what role, and when. Each step follows a published rule.</p><a class="lk" href="/audit-evidence-pack">Open the audit evidence pack <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      <ul class="kp-l" aria-label="Checks on example record MDF-000033"><li><time>9 Nov</time><span>Approved by Grace Adeyemi</span><b class="tag ctl">Rule C-01</b></li><li><time>16 Nov</time><span>Ready</span><b class="tag ctl">Rule C-08</b></li><li><time>11 Dec</time><span>Invoice approved</span><b class="tag ctl">Rule C-11</b></li></ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- 5 · Close: one block of solid indigo -->
<section class="close" id="walkthrough" aria-labelledby="h-close"><div class="in">
  <div class="blk pv"><h2 id="h-close">See the rules<br>on your own process.</h2><p>We'll walk one request through with your approval route and your evidence checklist.</p><a class="btn white" href="/request-a-walkthrough">Request a walkthrough</a></div>
  <ul class="qs"><li><a href="/how-it-works">How it works</a></li><li><a href="/audit-evidence-pack">Open the audit evidence pack</a></li><li><a href="/#roles">Built for every role</a></li></ul>
</div></section>

</main>

<script>
  import "../scripts/controls.js";
</script>
</Base>
